# Contabo soft CPU pin — kube play does not persist HostConfig
# CpusetCpus or process nice. Re-applied after /health by
# scripts/apply-fullstack-soft-pin.sh.
#
# Host snapshot (Release, locked): nproc=6, CPUs 0–5.
#
# Live fullstack pin stays 2-5 / nice -5 UNTIL cutover. Do not shrink
# it in this draft. Sidecar stays unpinned (do not steal send cores
# for MoQ). Floki MOVE is forbidden — Contabo → Floki TS only.
#
# Bot/music unit — packaging option (1), intra-container affinity:
#   TS6_BOT_CPUSET / TS6_BOT_SEND_CPUSET=0-1 pins Voice *send threads*
#   inside ts6-manager-music (sched_setaffinity on voice-rt).
#   A whole-container `podman update --cpuset-cpus=0-1` would also pin
#   ffmpeg/yt-dlp onto send cores and violates Music's "off 0-1".
#   With fullstack occupying 2-5, media workers cannot get exclusive
#   non-0-1 cores without overlapping fullstack. They stay unpinned
#   (TS6_BOT_DECODE_CPUSET unset) and may contend on 0-1 with send
#   (and with Scuffed / host noise) until seats + FrozenTear approve
#   shrinking fullstack or freeing a third slice.
#
# TS6_BOT_NICE is applied to the music container pid (optional) and
# also to voice-rt threads. TS6_BOT_CONTAINER_CPUSET stays empty —
# do not container-pin 0-1.

TS6_FULLSTACK_CPUSET=2-5
TS6_FULLSTACK_NICE=-5

TS6_BOT_CPUSET=0-1
TS6_BOT_SEND_CPUSET=0-1
TS6_BOT_NICE=-5
# TS6_BOT_CONTAINER_CPUSET=
# TS6_BOT_DECODE_CPUSET=

# TS6_SIDECAR_CPUSET=
# TS6_SIDECAR_NICE=
